## Instructions

The following instructions have been attached to this task:

### native-demo-brief.md
> Concrete UI direction

Keep Notes as the main demo. Prefer search, clear note editing and deletion, meaningful seeded notes and a simple pinned/favorite option if it fits the existing service. Use List, Section, Form, toolbar, searchable, system sheets, SF Symbols and semantic typography/colors. No custom design system, gradients or ornamental glass cards. Use glass button style on a meaningful primary control behind iOS/macOS 26 availability, with standard bordered fallback. Local draft/search state may live in presentation; domain mutations dispatch in containers only. Keep data in memory and clearly explain demo behavior rather than adding persistence/network scope. SwiftUI expert latest-apis and liquid-glass references apply. Validate a complete create/edit/search/delete journey visually, including older runtime if installed. Parent observed Notes obtain failure currently returns success; audit task will address upstream patterns first.


### review-focus.md
> Review scope for UI work

Keep this a small teaching app, not a framework exercise. All public prose and code comments English. Preserve iOS 17 and macOS 14 deployments. Latest APIs supported by installed Xcode 26.5 are sufficient; do not target betas. Read current upstream ReluxUI protocols before deciding props/state patterns. Existing main menu/auth/account screens need coherent native styling as well as notes. Verify native accessibility labels, Dynamic Type, and keyboard behavior. Update inline comments where the user learns action -> flow/service -> reducer -> UI projection. Do not add arbitrary delays or testing-only behavior to product logic.




